{"language_code":"eng","language_probability":0.9667292833328247,"text":"Great. I can start with the beta if that works for everyone. So the beta went out on Monday to about 200 people. Switching themes now takes under a second, even on the old ThinkPad. Dead. The one thing still open is the preview on high-resolution screens. The thumbnails look blurry at scale two. I looked at that yesterday. We render them at the wrong size. I can fix it today. It's one line in the shell. Wait, is that the same bug we had with the wallpapers last month? Similar, but not the same code. The wallpaper one was the cache. Half a day, maybe less, then Ana can test it tomorrow morning. Tomorrow morning works for me. Can I add something about the installer? We changed the second screen, and the numbers look really good. Installs finish in 40 seconds now, down from 90. People stop at the disk encryption step much less now that we explain why it matters. That is a big jump. It is. I want to do the same for the keyboard layout question next week. No, it's only text and one picture. Tyler can do that without me. One more thing, the plugin review for the weather widget is still pending. It has been four days now. Nothing yet. I'll ping them this afternoon. If it's not merged by Thursday, we should ship the theme picker without it. Sounds good. Perfect. Thanks, everyone.","words":[{"text":"Great.","start":6.28,"end":6.72,"type":"word","logprob":-0.00004835592092907367},{"text":" ","start":6.72,"end":6.72,"type":"spacing","logprob":-0.633042573928833},{"text":"I","start":7.16,"end":7.2,"type":"word","logprob":-4.768370445162873e-7},{"text":" ","start":7.2,"end":7.24,"type":"spacing","logprob":-1.1920928244535389e-7},{"text":"can","start":7.24,"end":7.44,"type":"word","logprob":-1.1920928244535389e-7},{"text":" ","start":7.44,"end":7.56,"type":"spacing","logprob":-1.1920922133867862e-6},{"text":"start","start":7.56,"end":7.82,"type":"word","logprob":-1.1920922133867862e-6},{"text":" ","start":7.